      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Those neck tilt ones seem to be \"neckfixed\". Which is bad in the current state.\nWhat the current full body ssystem does(from what I can tell) is that it lets the head bone(and I think chest + spine bones too) move around freely to be able to match the head location. The only things stretching are the inbetweens, so where the weightpaint of the head and neck meet as example.\nThe Chest-Neck angle seems unnatural cause of the neckfix, I dont get that on the chest with my avatars, only a slightly stretched neck at times.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
